  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Field Register",
    "overview": "ImpactLens is a register of field evidence set on a warm near-black ground. The org's own photographs are the brightest things on the screen; everything else is tonal: panels one step lighter than the ground, hairline edges, bone text in five steps of warmth. One ember accent is spent where something is committed or selected, and nowhere else.\n\nEvidence leads. Home opens on a photo hero carrying one sentence of state (\"1 asset is waiting for review.\") and four running totals, then gives the widest column to the next item to review, drawn large enough to check the photo against the AI's reading of it. Every asset carries an accession number in mono and one of three evidence marks. Numbers are tabular so columns of confidence and counts line up like a ledger.\n\nDark is the default theme (`next-themes`, `defaultTheme=\"dark\"`). A light theme is derived from the same roles: warm paper ground, white sheets, a deeper ember that holds contrast on white. The system refuses the icon-KPI-card dashboard: totals are set as plain type over the evidence, not as tiles with icons.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm near-black ground with tonal panels a step up; depth from tone and hairlines, not shadow.",
      "One ember accent, rationed to commit actions, selection, focus, and the verified stamp.",
      "Real field photographs as the hero material; no illustration, no stock gradients standing in for evidence.",
      "Accession numbers (`A·XXXXXX`) in Geist Mono; everything else in Public Sans.",
      "Tabular figures on every count, percentage, and score.",
      "Generous rounding on containers (16px panels, 12px media) over square controls-sized corners (8px)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Ember Budget Rule",
        "body": "Ember is spent on exactly four things: commit actions, selection (active nav icon, active tab underline, review count badge), the focus ring, and the verified stamp. Progress bars, charts of volume, decorative icons and headings stay neutral. If a screen has two ember buttons, one of them is wrong.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Evidence Is The Colour Rule",
        "body": "The only saturated hues on screen besides ember are the org's photographs and the fixed UN SDG identity colours in SDG coverage. No other hue is introduced as decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Dark Ink On Ember Rule",
        "body": "Text and glyphs on an ember fill use Ember Ink, never white.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Mono Means Identifier Rule",
        "body": "Geist Mono is only for accession numbers and key hints. Never for headings, labels, or numbers that are measurements.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ledger Figures Rule",
        "body": "Every count, percentage, score and rank is set with tabular figures so stacked values align.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence Case Rule",
        "body": "Headings, labels and buttons are sentence case at their natural tracking. Hierarchy comes from size and weight, not from uppercase tracked micro-labels.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Nothing Floats Rule",
        "body": "At rest, nothing on the page casts a shadow. Hover changes an edge or a tone, never elevation.",
        "section": "elevation"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Photo Carries Light Rule",
        "body": "The brightest pixels on a screen belong to field photographs; the hero fades its photo into the ground with gradients so text always sits on the dark side, never over the image's detail.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do keep ember to commit actions, selection, the focus ring and the verified stamp; one ember button per view.",
      "Do put text on ember in ember-ink (`#1c0f06`), never white.",
      "Do build depth from ground, panel and raised tones with 1px hairlines; strengthen the hairline on hover.",
      "Do show an accession number (`A·XXXXXX`, Geist Mono 11px) wherever an asset is named.",
      "Do mark evidence state with the three Evidence Marks, each with its text label for assistive tech.",
      "Do set every count, percentage and score in tabular figures.",
      "Do lead with the org's own verified photographs; fade them into the ground so text sits on dark.",
      "Do round panels 16px, media 12px, controls 8px, tags 6px."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't fill progress bars, volume charts or decorative icons with ember; they use bar-neutral.",
      "Don't set totals as icon-topped KPI cards; set them as plain type in a row.",
      "Don't introduce hues other than ember, caution, destructive and the fixed UN SDG colours.",
      "Don't use mono for headings, labels or measurements.",
      "Don't add shadows to resting panels or cards, or lift on hover.",
      "Don't put uppercase tracked micro-labels or eyebrows above headings."
    ]
  }
